# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js application (v16.0.10 with App Router).

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/speed-insights` (v1.3.1)
- **Method**: Installed using npm
- **Files Modified**:
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

### 2. Layout Configuration
- **File Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Imported `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after `{children}`
  
### Implementation Details
Since this is a Next.js 16.0.10 project using the App Router:
- Used the Next.js-specific import: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Placed the component in the root layout to track all pages
- The component is positioned at the end of the body tag for optimal performance
- No additional configuration needed (the component auto-detects the route)

## Verification Results

### ✓ Build Test
- Ran `npm run build` successfully
- All routes compiled without errors
- Production build completed in ~5.4s

### ✓ Linter Test
- Ran `npm run lint`
- No linting errors introduced in `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Pre-existing linter warnings in other files remain unchanged

### ✓ TypeScript Compilation
- TypeScript compilation passed during build
- No type errors introduced

## Notes
- The Speed Insights component will automatically track Web Vitals metrics
- Metrics will be visible in the Vercel dashboard when deployed
- No additional environment variables or configuration required
- The implementation follows Vercel's official documentation for Next.js 13.5+
